  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "id": "xu-zhimo-poems-s0012-p00012",
      "source_en": "I too would praise this wondrous universe, I too would wish to forget that sorrow lives among human beings, like a plum-blossom sparrow unburdened by any weight, singing in the clear morning, leaping at dusk— and if only that breeze-like purity would stay by my side always! I also long my verses to flow like clear water, I also long my heart to drift, slow and lingering, like a fish in a pond. But now my heart is all greasy fire and burning flame, do not ask me again of leisurely poetic feeling. — God! You do not return her life and freedom, even in a single day! Composed in August, 1925.",
